<title>BELGIUM: Textile union protests Indian union leader killing.</title>
<headline>Textile union protests Indian union leader killing.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Brussels-based international textile union on Thursday condemned the killing of an Indian trade union leader and called on the Indian government to catch the murderers.</p>
<p>&quot;The bullets might have silenced Samant but they will not quiet those demanding justice for the thousands who struggle to secure a livelihood from Bombay's textile industry,&quot; Neil Kearney, General Secretary of the International Textile, Garment and Leather Workers' Federation said in a statement.</p>
<p>Well-known Indian trade union leader Datta Samant was killed by unidentified gunmen on Thursday, police said earlier.</p>
<p>Samant shot into fame in the early 1980s as a fiery union leader who led a prolonged textile strike in Bombay.</p>
</text>
